    "narrative": "Ghost Ride the WHIP enters today with a potent lineup anchored by **Josh Naylor**, who leads our squad with a 77.11 efficiency score. Facing Trevor Rogers (4.34 xERA), **Josh Naylor** benefits from a massive 16% park adjustment and favorable winds blowing out, setting up a high-ceiling day for RBI production. Close behind is **James Wood** (74.97) and **Seiya Suzuki** (74.67). **James Wood** is a must-start despite the threat of a quick catcher, as his elite 0.404 xwOBA and top-of-the-order positioning outweigh the risk of being caught stealing. **Seiya Suzuki** rounds out our primary targets, enjoying a significant boost from a hitter-friendly environment and a favorable matchup against Tomoyuki Sugano.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Kyle Karros** (56.29) on the bench. While his score was bolstered by a 14% park advantage at home, the optimizer ultimately favored the positional flexibility and higher floor provided by **Tyler Soderstrom** and **Max Muncy**. **Max Muncy** (69.14) remains a strong play in the utility slot, capitalizing on a weak matchup against Robert Gasser, which more than offsets his middle-of-the-order positioning. Conversely, we are exercising extreme caution with **Dalton Rushing** (40.24); facing Paul Skenes is a brutal assignment, and his score is depressed by a 19% SP skill penalty. He stays in the lineup only due to positional scarcity, but he is at the absolute floor for active status today.\n\nManagers should monitor the status of **Jose Caballero** (57.26) closely. Although he provides essential stolen base upside, his score was hit by a 13% platoon penalty, and the lower-order batting position limits his run-scoring opportunities. We are also wary of **Dalton Rushing** and **Alex Freeland**\u2014who remains benched with a sub-40 score\u2014as both are staring down the elite stuff of Paul Skenes. Ensure all lineups are confirmed before game time, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status across our roster adds an inherent layer of volatility to these projections.",
